Package: dirtree
Title: Directory-Style Taxonomy Trees as ggplot Axis Labels
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Language: en-US
Authors@R: person("Hood", "Z. J.", , "zjardynhood@example.invalid", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Draws ranked hierarchies, such as microbial taxonomy from phylum to
    genus, as directory-style elbow trees that replace flat axis labels in
    'ggplot2'. A lineage table with one row per leaf and one column per rank is
    collapsed to unique tree paths; each axis break becomes a node indented by
    rank depth, joined to its parent by the elbow connectors of the 'LaTeX'
    'dirtree' package, with identical lineages collapsed to a '× N' multiplier.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
